<BaseLayout title="IPC" description="SIGRUN inter-process communication: capability-guarded channel endpoints, lock-free SPSC message queues, bitmask notifications, and shared memory with derived rights.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Subsystem 7 · ipc</p>
  <h1>IPC: channels, messages, notifications, shared memory</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A microkernel lives or dies by its IPC. SIGRUN gives you four primitives: synchronous
    <strong>channels</strong> between two endpoints, small <strong>messages</strong> that can carry
    capabilities, asynchronous <strong>notifications</strong> as a 256-bit signal set, and
    <strong>shared memory</strong> for zero-copy bulk transfer.
  </p>

  <h2>A channel is two endpoints and two queues</h2>
